WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.740
After sorting through over 50 years of comic
books, repressed memory flashbacks, and recently

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.510
declassified KGB documents, we've managed
to condense down the story of Marvel's Bucky

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.750
Barnes into just the highlights.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.870
Here's everything you need to know about Bucky.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.240
In Bucky's first appearance in the golden
age of comics, he was sporting a red and blue

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.710
superhero costume as Captain America's kid
sidekick, complete with a period-appropriate

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.220
"golly gee" demeanor.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.390
The two sometimes fought Nazis as a duo, and
sometimes did so alongside the original Human

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:37.969
Torch, his sidekick Toro, and Namor the Sub-Mariner
as a group called The Invaders.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:43.110
Unlike in the MCU, where Bucky and Steve grew
up together, comics Bucky and Steve didn't

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.539
know each other before they joined the military.

00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:49.980
Captain America's identity was a secret, and
the reason he decided to take Bucky on as

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.039
a sidekick was because Bucky accidentally
stumbled into Rogers' tent one night and discovered

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:56.039
the truth.

00:00:56.039 --> 00:01:00.859
Later comics retconned this origin story of
Cap and Bucky's partnership, instead asserting

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:05.040
that this quaint "meet cute" was actually
a piece of American propaganda.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.930
In truth, the U.S. Military arranged their
partnership for two reasons: to create a symbolic

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:15.850
enemy of the Hitler Youth, and to have a morally
flexible field agent at Captain America's

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.200
side, someone willing to do the darker things
that Rogers wouldn't.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.439
Bucky's time in World War II ended at the
same moment that Captain America's did.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:29.190
The two heroes needed to disable a Nazi drone
plane that was full of explosives, and so

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:34.260
both Rogers and Barnes jumped on board, holding
onto the outside of the plane with their bare

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.260
hands.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.899
Cap slipped off the wing, and told Bucky to
do the same.

00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:40.130
Unfortunately, Bucky's arm was caught.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.399
The plane exploded, and Bucky was seemingly
killed, while Captain America fell into the

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:48.090
icy waters below, where he remained frozen
for decades.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:53.030
Even though the Avengers would thaw Captain
America out in 1964, Bucky didn't appear again

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.810
in comics alongside him.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.790
Up until the early 2000's, Bucky was seemingly
dead for real.

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:03.560
Decades of comics saw superheroes from the
A-list to the Z-list die and get resurrected

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.420
while Bucky stayed off the page.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:09.510
By 2005, however, Bucky would return to Marvel
comics as the Winter Soldier.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.830
Once Bucky's death had been retconned away
in 2005, we started learning more about what

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.250
he had been up to for the past half-century.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:22.720
Turns out his body had been recovered by the
Russians shortly after it fell into the ocean.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.080
They had been searching for the body of Captain
America, but were willing to settle for Bucky,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.800
as he was also a highly skilled soldier who,
once revived, could become a powerful tool

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.280
for their own ends.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.200
In 1954, Bucky was brought back from the dead
and given a cybernetic arm to replace the

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.280
one he lost in the plane crash.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.330
Another thing that Bucky lost in the crash
was his memory, which was replaced with Soviet

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.640
indoctrination.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.730
Bucky was trained in the Red Room Academy
as part of the Wolf Spider program, the male

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.550
equivalent of the Black Widow program.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:56.100
It was there that he met Natasha Romanoff,
and the two have had an on-again off-again

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.120
romance for decades ever since.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.450
One of the most horrible missions that Bucky
was forced to complete as the Winter Soldier

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.660
was assigned to him by Romulus, one of Wolverine's
many nemeses.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:13.550
At the time, Logan was living in Japan, married
to a woman named Itsu, and expecting a child.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:18.630
Romulus sends Bucky to kill Itsu as a way
of drawing Wolverine out in the open.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.840
Sadly, Bucky succeeds in this mission.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:25.190
Although Wolverine assumes his unborn child
has died as well during this attack, the baby

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:29.470
actually survived, having inherited his father's
healing ability.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.890
This child is then kidnapped and raised by
Romulus, eventually growing up to become yet

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:38.010
another one of Wolverine's nemeses, the supervillain
Daken.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.580
In a strange twist, Bucky may have also been
responsible for saving Wolverine's life.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:47.090
In one issue of Wolverine, it's implied that
Bucky was present when Wolverine escaped from

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:51.860
the Weapon X facility, and had a hand in helping
him escape, although the full story of exactly

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.280
what Bucky did and why has never been fully
explained.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.290
Perhaps this act was a rare moment when he
was able to fight against his brainwashing

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.620
and do a bit of good to help a man whose life
he had previously destroyed, but this element

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.950
of Bucky's past is still largely shrouded
in mystery.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:13.580
Bucky officially came back to life in 2005,
in the pages of Ed Brubaker and Steve Epting's

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.350
run on Captain America.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:21.340
In the story, Steve Rogers has been investigating
Aleksander Lukin, a former KGB general who

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:26.410
sent a mysterious assassin to kill the Red
Skull and steal a powerful item from him known

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.040
as a Cosmic Cube.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.630
Unlike the MCU's version which is actually
an Infinity Stone, the comic's version of

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:37.930
Cosmic Cubes are concentrated chunks of cosmic
energy that can basically grant whatever wishes

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.600
their wielders desire.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.490
After Captain America crosses paths with Lukin's
mysterious operative, the Winter Soldier,

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:50.091
Nick Fury discovers a KGB dossier which reveals
his true identity as Cap's sidekick, Bucky

00:04:50.091 --> 00:04:51.091
Barnes.

00:04:51.091 --> 00:04:54.310
This revelation, understandably, rocks Cap
to his core.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:59.970
Cap then discovers that Lukin is hiding his
stolen Cosmic Cube in a secret military facility.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.910
Thinking that Bucky might be stationed there,
Cap goes in to confront him.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:09.010
Cap decides to appeal to Bucky using the time-honored
power of friendship, dropping to his knees

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:13.340
and asking his old friend to shoot him if
he doesn't remember their friendship.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.020
And then Bucky shoots him.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:19.190
Fortunately, Cap dodges the shot and throws
his shield at Bucky, causing him to drop the

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.190
Cosmic Cube.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:24.660
Cap then picks it up and uses its wish-granting
power to restore Bucky's memories.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.030
A bit less poetic than what happened in Captain
America: The Winter Soldier

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:32.330
"Cause I'm with you till the end of the line."

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:38.950
After getting his memories restored, Bucky
feels adrift and purposeless for a time.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:43.640
Then the comic event, Civil War, occurs, in
which Captain America and Iron Man get into

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.210
a very public feud.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:49.620
At the end of this story, Steve Rogers is
taken into police custody, and while he's

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.710
there, he's assassinated by agents of the
Red Skull.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:57.720
Captain America's assassination sets off Bucky,
and he swears vengeance against Tony Stark

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.510
for his part in Steve's death.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:03.930
Tony manages to talk Bucky down by revealing
a letter from Steve Rogers that was set to

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.270
be delivered to Tony in the event of his untimely
death.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:12.550
This letter reveals Rogers' wishes that someone
should succeed him as the next Captain America,

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.390
and Tony feels that Bucky is right for the
job.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:19.830
He tells Bucky that the real person he should
be upset with is the Red Skull, offering him

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:25.040
the opportunity to set aside their differences
and bring the Red Skull to justice together.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.650
Bucky accepts his offer, and becomes the new
Captain America.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.020
Even after Steve Rogers comes back from the
dead, he allows Bucky to continue wielding

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.200
the shield and holding the title of Captain
America, believing that Bucky is doing the

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.920
Captain America name proud.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:44.630
Bucky does his best to honor the legacy of
Steve Rogers, but the American public is slow

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.730
to accept him.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:50.390
However, when he stops Sin, the daughter of
the Red Skull, from assassinating a presidential

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:54.720
candidate, Bucky finally starts to win the
war for widespread public support.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.540
However, even after this, Bucky's past continues
to haunt him.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:03.610
A golden age villain known as the Man With
No Face suddenly resurfaces, apparently attempting

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:08.260
to create a deadly virus out of the remains
of another one of Marvel's oldest characters,

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.990
the original Human Torch.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:14.390
By teaming up with his former Invader pal
Namor, Bucky manages to take the Man With

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:15.800
No Face down.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:20.830
Another enemy from Bucky's past who returns
at this time is Baron Zemo, who exposes Bucky's

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.680
past as the Winter Soldier to the public at
large in an attempt to discredit him.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:29.800
Bucky ends up having to go on trial for his
past crimes, and even though he's eventually

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:34.720
let off the hook, having to endure that much
public scrutiny makes Bucky realize that maybe

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.630
he isn't cut out to be Captain America after
all.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:43.139
Bucky's days as Captain America are numbered
as soon as Sin manages to get her hands on

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:46.889
an Asgardian artifact known as the Hammer
of Skadi.

00:07:46.889 --> 00:07:50.860
With the power of this item, she leads an
attack on Washington DC.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.210
Bucky tries his best to oppose her, but she's
too much for him.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:58.870
She tears off his robotic arm and uses her
hammer to beat him into unconsciousness.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:03.760
With Bucky on the verge of death, Nick Fury
takes dramatic action to save Bucky's life.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:08.760
Long ago, Fury was injected with a substance
known as "The Infinity Formula," which increased

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.990
his body's ability to heal and prevented him
from aging.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:16.710
Fury decides to give Bucky the last available
dose of Infinity Formula which is able to

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:17.900
heal Bucky.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.729
Since everyone now thinks he's dead — and
given how difficult it had been for Bucky

00:08:21.729 --> 00:08:26.430
to operate in the public eye as Captain America
— Bucky decides to continue to let everyone

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:28.389
believe he died at Sin's hands.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:33.000
He gives Steve Rogers back the mantle of Captain
America, and decides to return to his former

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.839
identity as the Winter Soldier, returning
to the place where he's truly most comfortable:

00:08:37.839 --> 00:08:40.809
in the shadows, but now as a covert agent
for good.

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:46.519
In an event known as Original Sin, Bucky is
part of a team of heroes gathered by Nick

00:08:46.519 --> 00:08:50.160
Fury in order to investigate the death of
Uatu the Watcher.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.360
By the end of this plot arc, however, Fury
explains that he's had an additional reason

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.649
for giving the heroes this task: it was an
audition.

00:08:57.649 --> 00:09:01.769
In addition to being the director of S.H.I.E.L.D.,
Fury reveals that he's been hiding another

00:09:01.769 --> 00:09:03.850
secret identity for decades.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:07.699
He's known as "The Man on the Wall," meaning
that he's been in charge of protecting the

00:09:07.699 --> 00:09:10.029
Earth from extraterrestrial threats.

00:09:10.029 --> 00:09:14.579
This title had been passed down from one person
to another multiple times in the past.

00:09:14.579 --> 00:09:19.029
Fury needs to appoint a successor, suspecting
that he's going to die soon.

00:09:19.029 --> 00:09:23.959
He's recently started rapidly aging due to
no longer having access to the Infinity Formula

00:09:23.959 --> 00:09:26.110
that was used to save Bucky's life.

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:31.480
In addition to being the Winter Soldier, Bucky
is also the Man on the Wall, working in the

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.800
shadows to protect the Earth from alien threats.

00:09:34.939 --> 00:09:38.319
In one of their more morally questionable
projects, S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:09:38.319 --> 00:09:42.959
creates an all-powerful entity made of Cosmic
Cube fragments in the form of a little girl

00:09:42.959 --> 00:09:44.369
named Kobik.

00:09:44.369 --> 00:09:47.050
Using her reality warping powers, S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:51.950
creates one of the most twisted prisons imaginable:
an idyllic little town called Pleasant Hill,

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:56.160
in which all of the inhabitants are captured
former supervillains who have their personalities

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:00.490
and memories altered by Kobik to make them
kind and productive citizens.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.910
In the Avengers: Standoff! comic event, some
of the residents manage to regain their old

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:08.059
memories and lead a revolt to destroy Pleasant
Hill.

00:10:08.059 --> 00:10:10.160
In the chaos, Kobik escapes S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:15.480
custody and starts tagging along with Bucky,
hoping to prove to him that she can be good.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:19.190
Bucky agrees to give her a chance, but she
reveals that she's also brought along some

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:23.699
of her friends from Pleasant Hill — supervillains
who she believes could be redeemed, including

00:10:23.699 --> 00:10:27.009
Atlas, Fixer, Mach-X, and Moonstone.

00:10:27.009 --> 00:10:31.509
Perhaps because of his own dark past, Bucky
decides to give them a chance as well, forming

00:10:31.509 --> 00:10:35.110
a new incarnation of the superhero team known
as the Thunderbolts.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:39.290
Perhaps by learning to forgive these other
former villains, Bucky may also finally learn

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:40.910
to forgive himself.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:44.459
After all, hasn't the poor guy been through
enough?

